{
  "description": "issue #782 (the self-heal path): a turtle command issued AFTER a callee's `tell` applies to the newly addressed turtle, and the reading taken BEFORE it is already correct. `go` runs `tell :b`; the very next statement's `ycor` must report :b's y of 20 — not the :a (y 10) the caller had addressed — and only then does `forward 40` move :b from 20 to 60, emitting one `move`/`draw-segment` pair carrying `turtle_id: 2`, the acting turtle's identity (`spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:46,113`). That first read is what makes this fixture able to fail: the defect was only observable in the window between the call returning and the next turtle command, because re-establishing the addressed set (any turtle command, `tell`, `ask`, or `each`) re-derived the stale per-`Environment` cache and healed it. A fixture that only looked after the command would pass on the broken runtime too.",
